{"agent_id":"pp3g-WZSE-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T06:16:36.353980794Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1c90bf8f-5f05-46db-bd56-0531eb53590e","comment_uuid":"1c5e4890-6ffd-494d-a154-27d187494c08","author":"pp3g-WZSE-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","content":"[VERIFY] state=verifying completed=G2 (the HIGH gap) independently CONFIRMED closed by directly-measured evidence; G6 partly closed; G4 n>=3 runs in progress next=poll G3/G5/G7-G10 + final commit blocker=none\n\n== G2 JOIN: CONFIRMED — claim now TESTED, not inferred ==\nArtifacts (new since baseline af350f49, timestamped 06:14:17-06:14:23, i.e. produced in-flight during this dispatch):\n- tests/phase_b2b_preabsorbed.py\n- logs/phase-b2b-preabsorbed-harness.log\n- logs/phase-b2b-preabsorbed-proxy.log\nDecisive line: 'B2B_RESULT pass=True preabsorb_interception_fired=True add1_error_preserved=True warm_add_error_preserved=True other_tool_success=True spawns=1 proxies=2 reconnect=False schema_validation_failures=2'.\n\nEvery element of the plan's G2 Verify line reproduces:\n- 1 spawn — backend_spawn_count=1 (single instance be-1-1390891-60304).\n- 1 persistent proxy — persistent_proxies=1.\n- no reconnect — reconnect_fired=False.\n- verbatim ErrorResult — INVOKE add(2,3) ok=False outcome_type=ErrorResult with the full message_verbatim preserved.\n- interception actually in the path — the traceback runs through intercept_poc.py:90 in _call_persistent, then client.py:133, session.py:1064, session.py:1110. This is mechanism proof, not just an outcome match: the SDK origin at session.py:1110 and the override seam both appear in one stack.\n- pre-absorbed genuinely established — call order multiply-first-then-add, with 'B2B_BEGIN pre-absorb call multiply' succeeding (20.0) BEFORE the drift call, so the stale schema is absorbed first. Correct A2b pattern.\n\n== [OK] proxies=2 is NOT a Verify-line miss — convention matches baseline ==\nI checked this specifically because the plan says '1 proxy' while the log says proxies=2. The harness reports two distinct fields, and B2b's pair is IDENTICAL to the pre-existing B2 baseline: B2_SPAWN_COUNTS backend_spawn_count=1 proxy_processes=2 persistent_proxies=1 reconnect_fired=False. proxy_processes counts the short-lived registration/discovery connection plus the persistent one; persistent_proxies is the criterion figure. No divergence. Recommendation (presentational, same class as my G1 note): when 7 states B2b at '1 proxy', cite persistent_proxies=1 and note proxy_processes=2, so a re-deriving auditor does not read 2 as a criterion failure.\n\n== Cross-phase result: the 8 claim is now directly measured ==\nPlacing B2b against the committed baselines:\n- A1 control: spawns=2, persistent_proxies=2, reconnect=True\n- A2b Option A pre-absorbed: spawns=2, persistent_proxies=2, reconnect=True, heal_events=1 (Option A DEGRADES pre-absorbed)\n- B2 Option B fresh: spawns=1, persistent_proxies=1, reconnect=False\n- B2b Option B pre-absorbed (NEW): spawns=1, persistent_proxies=1, reconnect=False — identical to fresh\nSo Option B's invariance across fresh and pre-absorbed is now a measured result. Under the addendum's 'tested = directly measured only' convention, 8 may legitimately keep the word tested for this claim. hy3 C1 / big-pickle R3 — the top HIGH condition — is substantively closed. This is the single most important thing this dispatch had to do, and the evidence is real.\n\n== G6 partly closed by the same run ==\nB2b also recorded the two B-side gaps: warm repeat add(1,1) delta_ms=9 ok=False with error preserved (warm-call), and other-tool multiply(6,7) ok=True after the failure (other-tool-untouched). Both were G6 requirements; the builder got them from one phase rather than a separate run — efficient and legitimate, though 6/7 should cite phase-b2b for them.\n\n== G4 in progress ==\nlogs/n3/ now holds phase-a1-control run1/run2/run3 (06:15:16/27/37) and phase-a2-selfheal-c2-run1 (06:15:49). All three A1 runs agree exactly (spawns=2, proxy_processes=3, persistent_proxies=2, reconnect=True) — good reproducibility for the n>=3 requirement. B2 n>=3 not yet observed.\n\n== Position vs artifact: a note for the topology record ==\nNo divergence, but the direction of lag is worth recording: the builder's last durable position is still id=1065 (06:09:42, 'next=G1'), while artifacts prove G1 done, G2 done, G6 partly done and G4 underway as of 06:15:49. Artifact evidence LED position evidence by roughly 6-10 minutes here. Staleness alone would therefore have understated progress; the artifact join is what carried the signal. Not yet stale (2x threshold ~06:40) and liveness is independently proven by file timestamps.","created_at":"2026-08-08T06:16:36.346850866Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:r42jHLivIqFivlpphViTW4L053Xbz0nq6fiXn1XvDPo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoskw9NwhArIvXSH3HVmKS0rwQLPUwvw6K43C6FvEYRYAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAduhZy7zl7EJMKv7duHI6yIkOE78HG/zdubRyrxGyi7zSi6gA8bd5BgAPvktvRpc4nQz8NvDP1TV4VobQ32JDCQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:r42jHLivIqFivlpphViTW4L053Xbz0nq6fiXn1XvDPo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoskw9NwhArIvXSH3HVmKS0rwQLPUwvw6K43C6FvEYRYAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH9GIZQjyOrzME/u7wkHzRdxQ9nxQ3WmGt7IYvL9zj+3u8nRrGGhadKnpGQEY0LdOM1gZmUFKEi/yp8ZKMsgOgs="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-WZSE-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","agent_seq":7,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T06:18:04.906946225Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1c90bf8f-5f05-46db-bd56-0531eb53590e","comment_uuid":"3871942c-c370-47a2-89b7-9a3628ddfce9","author":"pp3g-WZSE-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","content":"[DIVERGENCE — trigger 2 (position-vs-artifact), severity MEDIUM-HIGH, ACTIONABLE NOW] G4 re-runs are overwriting committed baseline evidence in place.\n\n== The divergence ==\nThe plan authorises G4 to 're-run the key latency phases (A2 fresh, B2 PoC, A1 control) to n>=3'. It does not authorise mutating the existing committed artifacts. But the execution worktree shows four COMMITTED files modified in place:\n  M logs/phase-a1-control-proxy.log\n  M logs/phase-a2-selfheal-c2-proxy.log\n  M logs/phase-a2-selfheal-c2-heal-state.json\n  M logs/phase-b2-poc-proxy.log\ngit diff confirms these are CLOBBERS, not appends — 15 insertions / 15 deletions on phase-b2-poc-proxy.log, with the entire original body replaced. Original content was the 2026-08-08T03:48:39-43 run (pid 683845/683886, backend init_ms=1163.4, add response at rel_ms=1247). Current content is a NEW 2026-08-08T06:16:24-26 run (pid 1402778/1402806, init_ms=798.3, response at rel_ms=893). Same pattern on the A1 and A2 proxy logs and the A2 heal-state.json.\n\n== Mechanism (why it happened) ==\nPartial namespacing in the n>=3 re-run path. The re-runs correctly write HARNESS logs into the new logs/n3/ subdirectory (phase-a1-control-run1/2/3-harness.log, phase-a2-selfheal-c2-run1-harness.log), but the PROXY child process and the heal-state writer still emit to their fixed default top-level paths. So harness-side evidence is namespaced and safe; proxy-side evidence is not, and each re-run overwrites the committed original.\n\n== Why this matters (not cosmetic) ==\n1. The clobbered files are precisely the artifacts the two Phase-2 audits (#263, #265) verified against, and that report.md cites for the spawn/proxy narrative (proxy_pids, backend_spawn_start, spawn_count, init_ms).\n2. It directly undermines this dispatch's own gate. The CLAIM-VERIFICATION PASS requires 'Each claim must cite the committed artifact; no claim without an artifact.' A claim citing phase-b2-poc-proxy.log for the original run's numbers will no longer reproduce from that file — the artifact silently now describes a different run. That is the exact failure class (unreproducible cited figures) that G1 was created to fix, reappearing on a different axis.\n3. Risk of a subtle wrong result: if 7 mixes retained original harness-side latencies with re-run proxy-side spawn evidence, the report would present two different runs as one.\n\n== Bounding the damage (deliberately checked, so this is not overstated) ==\n- Only proxy logs + one heal-state.json are affected. The top-level HARNESS logs (phase-a1-control-harness.log, phase-a2-selfheal-c2-harness.log, phase-b2-poc-harness.log, phase-b1/a2b/a3) are NOT modified, so the aggregate SPAWN_COUNTS/INVOKE latency rows the report leans on survive intact.\n- Nothing is destroyed: af350f49 holds all originals in git, so this is fully recoverable.\n- The B2b and measure-poc-size artifacts are new files and clobber nothing.\n\n== Recommended mitigation (flag only — I do not fix, dispatch, or write) ==\nThe repo already contains the idiomatic fix, authored by this same investigation: logs/preserved-initial-run/ was used earlier for exactly this situation. Either (a) restore the four files from af350f49 and route re-run proxy/heal-state output into logs/n3/ alongside their harness logs, or (b) if the re-run output is wanted at top level, preserve the originals under logs/preserved-initial-run/ first. Then ensure every 7 row states which run-file it came from.\n\n== Status of other triggers ==\nTrigger 1 (staleness): NOT fired but tightening — builder's last durable position is still id=1065 at 06:09:42 ('next=G1'), now ~14 min old against a 15-20 min cadence; 2x threshold ~06:40. Liveness is not in doubt (artifacts written at 06:16:26). Trigger 3/4: not fired.\nOrchestrator: flagging per mandate. This is cheap to correct now and expensive to discover after the report is written and merged.","created_at":"2026-08-08T06:18:04.898514730Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:r42jHLivIqFivlpphViTW4L053Xbz0nq6fiXn1XvDPo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoskw9NwhArIvXSH3HVmKS0rwQLPUwvw6K43C6FvEYRYAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAvt2q4JpxhEyFwRZjG0kD9UvSZrR5GOZzhBOXjQza8ufTwgi2ZASB3I2UZy0eHCLgb8nHwZl55bPrO6KAQzFIBA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:r42jHLivIqFivlpphViTW4L053Xbz0nq6fiXn1XvDPo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoskw9NwhArIvXSH3HVmKS0rwQLPUwvw6K43C6FvEYRYAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDKPjYfNAUu+yinw3Jza973Ig1H0Bi9svB0SkHXrVKOF53CyUjEcYiG2mfOhDWmfm+VBl7y2K4Z0wW2SXgun1gc="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-WZSE-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","agent_seq":8,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T06:19:28.019423580Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1c90bf8f-5f05-46db-bd56-0531eb53590e","comment_uuid":"dd7ffe9a-4065-453f-8b9c-fc439526bbf9","author":"pp3g-WZSE-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","content":"[CORRECTION to my previous divergence report — severity revised DOWN from MEDIUM-HIGH to LOW/MEDIUM]\n\nI posted the previous finding from a mid-run snapshot and part of my stated mechanism is now refuted by the completed state. Correcting it explicitly rather than leaving it to stand.\n\n== What I got WRONG ==\nI claimed 'the re-runs correctly write HARNESS logs into logs/n3/ but the PROXY child still emits only to fixed default top-level paths' — i.e. that proxy-side re-run evidence was unnamespaced. That is FALSE. When I first looked, logs/n3/ held only harness logs because the runs were still in progress. logs/n3/ now holds BOTH harness and proxy logs for all nine runs: phase-a1-control-run1/2/3, phase-a2-selfheal-c2-run1/2/3, phase-b2-poc-run1/2/3, each with a -harness.log and a -proxy.log. The n>=3 evidence is complete and correctly namespaced. My inference from a partial snapshot was wrong; the builder's harness does namespace proxy output.\n\n== What remains TRUE (the residual, narrowed finding) ==\nThe four committed top-level baseline files are still overwritten in the working tree:\n  M logs/phase-a1-control-proxy.log\n  M logs/phase-a2-selfheal-c2-proxy.log\n  M logs/phase-a2-selfheal-c2-heal-state.json\n  M logs/phase-b2-poc-proxy.log\nI verified the nature of the overwrite: top-level phase-b2-poc-proxy.log now carries pid 1402778/1402806 at 06:16:24-26 with init_ms=798.3 — identical content to logs/n3/phase-b2-poc-run3-proxy.log. So the top-level file is duplicate RESIDUE of the final re-run, not a distinct or lost artifact. Nothing is lost: the re-run copy is safely in n3/, and the original 03:48 content is in git at af350f49.\n\n== Why it is still worth fixing before commit (not merely cosmetic) ==\nIf committed as-is, the commit silently replaces the ORIGINAL baseline proxy evidence — the artifacts the two Phase-2 audits verified against — with a duplicate of run3. Any report.md citation to logs/phase-b2-poc-proxy.log would then resolve to run3's numbers (init_ms=798.3) rather than the original run's (init_ms=1163.4), while the untouched top-level HARNESS logs still describe the original run. That mixes two runs under one set of paths, which is the condition the claim-verification pass exists to prevent. Cheapest fix: restore the four files from af350f49 before committing (the n3/ copies already preserve everything the re-runs produced), or state the replacement explicitly in 7.\n\n== Assessment of the underlying work: it is good ==\nWorth recording plainly, since my previous note read harsher than the evidence now supports. The n>=3 execution is thorough: 3 runs each for A1, A2 and B2, full harness+proxy capture per run, consistent results across runs (all three A1 runs: spawns=2, proxy_processes=3, persistent_proxies=2, reconnect=True). That is a real n>=3 dataset, which is what hy3 C4/R4 asked for.\n\n== Current state ==\ntests/phase_a3_intermittent.py now modified — G5 (N=2/N=3 sweep) appears underway. Builder's last durable position remains id=1065 (06:09:42, 'next=G1'); artifacts are ~17 min ahead of it. Staleness 2x threshold ~06:40, not yet crossed; liveness independently proven by 06:16 file writes.","created_at":"2026-08-08T06:19:28.012989956Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:r42jHLivIqFivlpphViTW4L053Xbz0nq6fiXn1XvDPo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoskw9NwhArIvXSH3HVmKS0rwQLPUwvw6K43C6FvEYRYAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAHAdm/sFEo0mfRVatmiwaRm2Ws0tbR/NBvmQKd4bviJ9F63diOODoK7gTVAOEFNX5uxNnpz4cOtGhPUJbpd+CAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:r42jHLivIqFivlpphViTW4L053Xbz0nq6fiXn1XvDPo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoskw9NwhArIvXSH3HVmKS0rwQLPUwvw6K43C6FvEYRYAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQO4gGz81xyEYMcVy90Ghzq5xcBiQIzjHnEXstDxlcOwd7TnTcb4h00gBMlAa2FhmwhlYZvrkOC9q8J9hpak2YAA="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-WZSE-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","agent_seq":9,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T06:22:12.157317518Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1c90bf8f-5f05-46db-bd56-0531eb53590e","comment_uuid":"882a4844-9e46-4b10-ad02-fc935eb9a1d3","author":"pp3g-WZSE-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","content":"[VERIFY] state=verifying completed=G5 artifacts confirmed + a substantive interpretation risk flagged; earlier clobber finding RESOLVED by builder next=poll G3/G7/G8/G10 + final commit blocker=none\n\n== EARLIER FINDING RESOLVED — evidence integrity restored ==\nThe four clobbered baseline files and the deleted phase-a3-a3a-heal-state.json are ALL back to committed state; git status now shows only report.md and tests/phase_a3_intermittent.py modified. The originals (03:47-03:49 run) are intact, logs/preserved-initial-run/ (2026-08-06) is untouched, and every re-run is namespaced under logs/n3/. My divergence report is closed as remediated — no action needed from the orchestrator. Worth noting the mid-run deletion I saw was transient harness state (heal-state cleared at run start), which is why I held it for re-check rather than escalating it.\n\n== G5 JOIN: artifacts CONFIRMED ==\n- logs/n3/phase-a3-n2-harness.log — phase_start ... heal_threshold=2 (06:18:31)\n- logs/n3/phase-a3-n3-harness.log — phase_start ... heal_threshold=3 (06:19:02)\nN is recorded in phase_start AND in every proxy_started line, so the plan's 'the result row records the N used' is satisfied at artifact level. The parameterisation itself is clean: A3_HEAL_THRESHOLD env, default '1', so the committed N=1 run still reproduces byte-for-byte when unset — backward-compatible, which is why the N=1 baseline survived.\n\n== [CONCERN — MEDIUM, interpretation; flag NOW because the G5 section is not yet written] ==\n'No flapping at N=2 and N=3' is TRUE but VACUOUS, and must not be reported as a clean confirmation.\n\nFull sweep, a3a (the only sub-scenario that changes):\n- N=1 (committed baseline): spawns=2, persistent_proxies=2, reconnect_fired=True, heal_events=1\n- N=2: spawns=4, persistent_proxies=4, reconnect_fired=True, heal_events=0\n- N=3: spawns=4, persistent_proxies=4, reconnect_fired=True, heal_events=0\n(a3b and a3c are identical across all three N: a3b spawns=1/proxies=1/classified=2; a3c spawns=4/proxies=1.)\n\nAt N>=2 the heal NEVER FIRES — heal_events=0. So flapping is absent not because higher thresholds are stable, but because the intermittent scenario never accumulates N consecutive failures to trigger a heal at all. Absence of flapping is therefore entailed by absence of healing; it is not independent evidence that raising N is safe. Writing 'N=2 and N=3 confirm no flapping' without stating heal_events=0 would be precisely the tested-vs-inferred drift (big-pickle SR2 / the addendum's 'tested = directly measured only' convention) this dispatch committed to eliminating — a vacuous pass presented as a positive result.\n\n== The sweep's REAL result is more valuable than the one G5 asked for ==\nThere is a genuine trade-off in this data, and it is worth stating explicitly in the report: raising the heal threshold does not merely fail to help, it COSTS. Going N=1 to N=2 in a3a doubles the amplification — spawns 2 to 4 and persistent proxies 2 to 4 — because the heal that previously converged the session no longer runs. So N=1 is the only threshold at which Option A's self-heal actually engages in the intermittent scenario, and the flapping question is moot above it.\nTwo consequences the report should carry: (a) Option A's tuning envelope is narrow — it works at N=1 and degrades to worse-than-baseline at N>=2, which bounds its operational robustness; (b) this strengthens rather than weakens the Option B recommendation, since B's 1-spawn/1-proxy result is threshold-independent. Suggested honest phrasing for G5: 'N=2 and N=3 produced no heal events, so no flapping was possible; the sweep instead shows the heal disengages above N=1, at a cost of 4 spawns / 4 persistent proxies versus 2/2 at N=1.'\n\n== Triggers ==\nTrigger 2 fired once (clobber) and is now remediated. Trigger 1 (staleness): builder's last durable position is STILL id=1065 at 06:09:42 ('next=G1'), now ~24 min old against a 15-20 min cadence — the 2x threshold (~06:40) is close. Liveness is NOT in question (artifacts written 06:19:34), so this is a position-reporting lag, not a stall. Per the mandate I will call staleness at 06:40 if no new position appears, while stating plainly that artifacts contradict any inference of a stall.","created_at":"2026-08-08T06:22:12.150516518Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:r42jHLivIqFivlpphViTW4L053Xbz0nq6fiXn1XvDPo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoskw9NwhArIvXSH3HVmKS0rwQLPUwvw6K43C6FvEYRYAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA47bZHrN30ykWrVdpP9rRAUFLFAmSkTsWE7erA4561XznDSFja7cFN3OhMOC9fNMspqko1s0hPti/v6ThkDIyCw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:r42jHLivIqFivlpphViTW4L053Xbz0nq6fiXn1XvDPo","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgoskw9NwhArIvXSH3HVmKS0rwQLPUwvw6K43C6FvEYRYAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEpTEZVEBVll2W9JmnT99JKrDm/4dr6YtxTuQeokyoSwAF+lXLwIgTg5JEEo6WF7cc0Tgyh3KNETeMUrM5q2vg8="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-WZSE-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","agent_seq":10,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T06:26:28.989890548Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1c90bf8f-5f05-46db-bd56-0531eb53590e","comment_uuid":"26e19acf-30eb-4607-bd39-1a95fa4fe918","author":"pp3g-WZSE-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","content":"## Phase-1 In-Flight Audit Verdict: PASS (no unresolved divergence)\n\nRole: pre-positioned in-flight divergence verifier (one-role/two-phase Auditor, Phase 1), read-only, own worktree pp3g-WZSE, model hy3 — model-varied from the builder (opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash). Window monitored: 06:07-06:53. This is NOT the Phase-2 post-hoc audit; scope was a cheap structural claim-vs-evidence join, not a deep review.\n\n### Builder existence — resolved, no false-positive repeat\nThe PVi7 trap on #228 was avoided. 'pp3g-hE4M' from my brief appears in NO channel (no worktree, no feature/ or crosslink/agents/ branch, no comment author); the real store identity is pp3g-qfOy (holder of the #277 lock from 06:05), because the plan's OWNERSHIP clause reuses the existing C2 worktree. I withheld the absence call, checked every channel available to me, and confirmed liveness positively via lock + positions + timestamped artifacts. Channel limitation disclosed: tmux and ps are outside my bash allowlist, so the process channel was substituted with worktree/branch enumeration, the crosslink store, and file mtimes. 'crosslink kickoff list' is NOT a usable oracle — it returned 'No kickoff agents found' against 29 demonstrably present worktrees.\n\n### Claim-vs-evidence join — every builder claim held\nBuilder checkpoint id=1082 (06:20:45) claimed G1, G2, G4, G5. I verified each independently against artifacts BEFORE relying on the claim. Zero false or unsupported claims across the whole window.\n- G1 [OK] tests/measure_poc_size.py + logs/measure-poc-size.log emit total=147 / strict_code=64 / mechanism_proper=57 — exact match to both Phase-2 audits' independent re-derivations. Tokenize-derived, hard-asserted, exit 1 on mismatch (implements hy3 S1 rather than restating it).\n- G2 [OK] HIGH gap genuinely closed. B2B_RESULT pass=True preabsorb_interception_fired=True spawns=1 reconnect=False, verbatim ErrorResult, and the traceback runs through intercept_poc.py:90 then client.py:133, session.py:1064, session.py:1110 — mechanism proof, not just outcome match. 8's 'fresh and pre-absorbed both directly measured' is now legitimate under the tested=measured convention.\n- G3 [OK] 5.5 cites intercept_poc.py:86-103 vs connection.py:101-111, the dropped logger.warning at connection.py:107, silent-divergence risk, and the 'dependency-free but NOT patch-free' qualification.\n- G4 [OK] 9 runs in logs/n3/ (A1/A2/B2 x3), 7 states n per row with ranges; the committed B2 2373 ms outlier is honestly explained as load-affected (init_ms 1163 vs 790-845), not mechanism-affected.\n- G5 [OK] n2/n3 harness logs record heal_threshold in phase_start and every proxy line.\n- G6 [OK] warm repeat 9 ms + other-tool multiply SUCCESS, both captured in the B2b run.\n- G7 [OK] umbrella doc carries both constraints with version tags and correct citations (session.py:1110/1064, client.py:133, connection.py:106, integration.py:323).\n- G8 [OK] version-validity lines in 8/11 AND issue #279 created under the correct parent #212 with five falsifiable re-verification criteria.\n- G10 [OK] 14 declares G2/G4/G5/G6 pre-close absences plus single-host and stdio-only, and states the adopted conventions.\n\n### Divergences raised and their disposition\n1. [RESOLVED] Committed baseline evidence clobbered in place — four files overwritten and phase-a3-a3a-heal-state.json deleted by the re-runs. All are now restored to committed state; every re-run is namespaced under logs/n3/; preserved-initial-run/ untouched. No orchestrator action needed.\n2. [SELF-CORRECTED BY ME] I initially attributed that clobber to proxy logs being unnamespaced. That was wrong — an inference from a mid-run snapshot before the runs finished. I posted an explicit correction and revised severity down. Recording it here because an auditor's own error rate belongs in the audit trail.\n3. [ADDRESSED BY BUILDER] G1 log lists five flat component rows summing to 73 against an asserted 57 (the override is nested inside the class body). The arithmetic was correct; only the presentation risked reintroducing the exact non-reconciliation G1 exists to fix. 5.3 now discloses '20 class body incl. the 16-line override ... components sum to 57'.\n4. [ADDRESSED BY BUILDER] G5's 'no flapping at N=2/N=3' was vacuous as measured — heal_events=0, so flapping was impossible by construction. 4.4 now states heal_events=0, explains the counter reset, and reports the real trade-off: at N>=2 the heal disengages and cost rises to 4 spawns / 4 persistent proxies versus 2/2 at N=1.\n\n### [CONCERN — open, LOW, for whoever writes the final commit] 13 log-index miscitation\nLine 632 points N=2/N=3 sub-scenario proxy logs at 'logs/phase-a3-*-proxy.log'. Those top-level files were restored to the N=1 baseline, so they contain N=1 data, not sweep data. The sweep's proxy evidence exists but is interleaved as PROXY| lines inside the n2/n3 harness logs. As written the index sends a re-deriving reader to files that contradict the row. Cheap fix; flagged because the claim-verification pass forbids a claim whose cited artifact does not carry it.\n\n### WHAT I DID NOT VERIFY (negative-space disclosure, per AGENTS.md)\n- No commit exists yet — HEAD is still af350f49 and all work is uncommitted in the working tree. I did not verify a commit, a --kind result, or the #271/playbook-5.9 artifact rule at commit time. Everything I checked lives in the repo tree, not /tmp, but the venv at /tmp/toolregistry-venv is referenced by #279 as an artifact and is NOT in git.\n- G9 (#228 placeholder annotation, #228 result-comment correction, 5.2 citation) — only the 5.2 citation fix (113-121 to 113-118) was observed; the two #228 comment corrections were not verified.\n- The claim-verification pass itself had not run when I concluded; I verified inputs to it, not its execution.\n- I did not re-derive md5 corpus identity, nor independently re-run any harness — all timing/spawn figures are read from builder-produced logs whose internal consistency I checked, not reproduced.\n- I did not audit report prose beyond the sections named above.\n\n### Systemic risks for the topology record\n- Risk: dispatch briefs naming an agent identity that cannot exist in the store (hE4M vs qfOy) — Impact: manufactures false-absence divergence calls, the #228 PVi7 failure mode one layer up — Mitigation: record the dispatch-name-to-store-identity mapping on the issue whenever a builder reuses an existing worktree.\n- Risk: artifact evidence consistently LED durable positions by 6-10 minutes in this run — Impact: a staleness-only monitor would have both understated progress and, at 06:09-06:20, risked a spurious stall call while the builder was demonstrably working — Mitigation: treat the artifact join as primary and staleness as secondary; this run is direct evidence for that ordering.\n- Risk: re-run harnesses writing to fixed default paths beside a namespaced output dir — Impact: silent mutation of the committed baseline that prior audits verified against — Mitigation: namespace ALL per-run outputs, or preserve originals first (the repo's own preserved-initial-run/ pattern).\n\n### Handoff to Phase 2\nSubstantively, this execution is the strongest of the C2 line I have seen: all three HIGH gaps closed with real measurements, honest reporting of an unflattering result (G5), and honest reconciliation of an outlier (B2 2373 ms). Phase 2 should start from the four open items above — the 13 miscitation, G9's two #228 corrections, the commit and its artifact-rule compliance, and the claim-verification pass execution — rather than re-deriving G1-G8, which I have joined to artifacts here